{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"620","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Professor GukiZ's Robot"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"0.5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Professor GukiZ makes a new robot. The robot are in the point with coordinates "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x1, y1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and should go to the point "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x2, y2)"},{"kind":"text","text":". In a single step the robot can change any of its coordinates (maybe both of them) by one (decrease or increase). So the robot can move in one of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"8"},{"kind":"text","text":" directions. Find the minimal number of steps the robot should make to get the finish position."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x1, y1"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":" - 109 ≤ x1, y1 ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the start position of the robot."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x2, y2"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":" - 109 ≤ x2, y2 ≤ 109"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the finish position of the robot."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"k